From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haze <patches@haze.invalid>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 12:14:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Turn on Global Privacy Control

Why: SPEC section 3 sends Sec-GPC: 1 and exposes navigator.globalPrivacyControl
by default. Chromium has both, behind the experimental GlobalPrivacyControlApi
feature and the UniversalOptOutSettings switch; this enables them, and the
default of the universal_optout.enabled pref comes from Haze's default prefs.
The setting stays a visible toggle in the cookie settings.
Security-relevant: yes
Security: Touches third_party/blink only to change the status of
GlobalPrivacyControlApi from experimental to stable. It adds a request header
and a read-only boolean; nothing about origin isolation or permissions changes.
Area: privacy
---
 components/universal_optout/features.cc                         | 2 +-
 .../blink/renderer/platform/runtime_enabled_features.json5      | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/components/universal_optout/features.cc b/components/universal_optout/features.cc
index 45aa2b2..667383d 100644
--- a/components/universal_optout/features.cc
+++ b/components/universal_optout/features.cc
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@ BASE_FEATURE(kUniversalOptOutExtension, base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 BASE_FEATURE(kUniversalOptOutExtensionSilent,
              base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
-BASE_FEATURE(kUniversalOptOutSettings, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+BASE_FEATURE(kUniversalOptOutSettings, base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
 BASE_FEATURE(kUniversalOptOutUpdateOnGeoLocationChanged,
              base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/runtime_enabled_features.json5 b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/runtime_enabled_features.json5
index bcf70f2..6591893 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/runtime_enabled_features.json5
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/runtime_enabled_features.json5
@@ -3674,7 +3674,7 @@
     {
       // Gates the navigator.globalPrivacyControl JavaScript API.
       name: "GlobalPrivacyControlApi",
-      status: "experimental",
+      status: "stable",
     },
     {
       name: "GlobalPrivacyControlForce",
